<html lang="en-US" xml:lang="en-US" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"> <head> <meta charset="utf-8"> <meta content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, user-scalable=yes" name="viewport"> <title>reply</title> </head> <body> <main> <h1 id="reply-to-reviewers">Reply to reviewers</h1> <div data-custom-style="Reply Header"> <p>
<strong>Title:</strong> Revised method</p> <p>
<strong>Manuscript Number:</strong> SNAPSHOT-2026-0001</p> <p>Thank you for the constructive comments.</p> </div> <p>
<br>
</p> <h2 id="reviewer-1">Reviewer 1</h2> <p>1. Please explain the revised method and compare it with prior work.</p> <div data-custom-style="Reply to Reviewers"> <p>
<em>Answer:</em>
</p> <p>We revised Section 2 (Line 7). The comparison follows [2,3], with the baseline from [1]. The bare citation [1] also identifies the baseline study. See Figure 2, Table 2, and Equation 2. The corresponding bracketed references are Figure 2 and Table 2.</p> <p>The revised excerpts are reproduced below.</p> <figure id="fig:revised"> <img alt="Figure 2 Revised trend." src="figure.svg"> <figcaption aria-hidden="true">Figure 2 Revised trend.</figcaption> </figure> <table data-alignment="center" data-autofit="window" data-cell_margin="0.10cm" id="tbl:revised"> <caption>Table 2 Revised scores.</caption> <thead> <tr> <th>Method</th> <th>Score</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Revised</td> <td>2</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>The following tables show horizontally, vertically, and jointly grouped results.</p> <table data-autofit="window"> <thead> <tr> <th>Method</th> <th>Score</th> <th>Notes</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td colspan="3">Horizontal group</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <table data-autofit="window"> <thead> <tr> <th>Method</th> <th>Score</th> <th>Notes</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td rowspan="3">Vertical group</td> <td>2</td> <td>First result</td> </tr> <tr> <td>3</td> <td>Second result</td> </tr> <tr> <td>4</td> <td>Third result</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <table data-autofit="window"> <thead> <tr> <th>Method</th> <th>Score</th> <th>Notes</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td colspan="2" rowspan="2">Combined group</td> <td>First result</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Second result</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>
<span class="display math"> \mathcal{L}(\theta) = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{j=1}^{N} \ell(y_j, \hat{y}_j) + \lambda R(\theta) \tag{2} </span>
</p> <p>where <span class="inline math">x</span> is the baseline score.</p> </div> <p>
<br>
</p> <p>2. Please identify the updated conclusion.</p> <div data-custom-style="Reply to Reviewers"> <p>
<em>Answer:</em>
</p> <p>The conclusion now states that the revised method improves the baseline (Line 13).</p> </div> </main> </body> </html>
